# Site documentation sync (`docs/`)

`docs/` describes the **live site at time T** — not career notes (`.cursor/infos/`) or future plans (`.cursor/plans/`).

## When to update

After any **delivered** change to stack, architecture, layout, or deployment, update the matching doc in the **same PR / session**. Do not defer.

| Change type | Update |
|-------------|--------|
| Dependencies, build scripts, tooling | [docs/tech-stack.md](../../docs/tech-stack.md) |
| New/split JS modules, data flow, render pipeline | [docs/architecture.md](../../docs/architecture.md) |
| HTML shell, CSS, responsive, vCard layout | [docs/layout-and-ui.md](../../docs/layout-and-ui.md) |
| GitHub Actions, `base` URL, hosting, costs | [docs/deployment.md](../../docs/deployment.md) |

## Out of scope for `docs/`

- **CV / pitch only** (`src/data/**`) → no `docs/` update unless rendering or i18n behavior changes.
- **Career recommendations** → `.cursor/infos/` or `.cursor/plans/`, not `docs/`.

## Checklist before finishing

1. Identify which doc(s) are affected.
2. Edit them to match the code — remove stale sections.
3. If `docs/INDEX.md` file list or zones change, update it too.

Index: [docs/INDEX.md](../../docs/INDEX.md)
